			<item>
				<title>How To add &#34;Open folder in Textmate&#34; to Finder Context Menu</title>
				<link>https://justaddwater.dk/2009/12/08/how-to-add-open-folder-in-textmate-to-finder-context-menu/</link>
				<pubDate>Tue, 08 Dec 2009 10:44:43 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://justaddwater.dk/2009/12/08/how-to-add-open-folder-in-textmate-to-finder-context-menu/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I wanted to add a menu item in Finder&amp;rsquo;s context menu that would open the selected folder in Textmate.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM.png&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM-289x300.png&#34; alt=&#34;Textmate context menu item: Open selected folder in  Textmate&#34; title=&#34;Textmate context menu item: Open selected folder in  Textmate&#34; class=&#34;aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1253&#34; height=&#34;300&#34; width=&#34;289&#34; srcset=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM-289x300.png 289w, https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM.png 366w&#34; sizes=&#34;(max-width: 289px) 100vw, 289px&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A google search suggested the method described by K. Adam Christensen on his blog: &amp;ldquo;&lt;a href=&#34;http://shifteleven.com/articles/2006/09/17/opening-a-directory-in-textmate-from-finder&#34;&gt;Opening a directory in TextMate from Finder&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rdquo;. However, from the documentation, I learned that that method is now outdated. Snow Leopard users should use &amp;ldquo;Services&amp;rdquo; and not &amp;ldquo;workflow&amp;rdquo; for setting this up.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
